  "goodToKnow": "Die Steinzeit is the Stone Age, followed by the Bronzezeit and Eisenzeit. Germany has important Stone Age finds: Neanderthal man from the Neandertal near Düsseldorf, and carved figures like the Venus vom Hohle Fels (about 40,000 years old) from the Swabian Jura caves, a UNESCO site. Figuratively, aus der Steinzeit means hopelessly outdated: Das ist ja Steinzeit! It has no plural."
